g more concerns about how she's  doing  the queen has cancelled her virtual  engagements as she deals with covid19  two days ago buckingham palace announced  the 95 year old had tested positive  she's said to be experiencing mild cold  like symptoms though as redmond shannon  reports the virus is a concern for  anyone her age  a jubilee queen still in covert 19  isolation as outside windsor castle her  english subjects prepared to ditch the  last of their pandemic laws  despite the palace repeating that the  queen only has mild symptoms the news  that the 95 year old monarch canceled  all her online engagements on tuesday is  a concern to some it's obviously such a  worry for anyone to get covered but  particularly as we know it does affect  people who are older but thankfully the  queen is triple vaccinated so hopefully  she will have a mild dose and she'll get  over it very soon rachel loftus came to  windsor castle to receive a royal honor  for her services to the clinically  vulnerable during the pandemic only to  arrive when the queen herself was  isolating it was lovely that she wanted  to do some light duties but we would we  would encourage everyone to treat this  virus take it very seriously and look  after themselves i do think it's  significant that the palace have put out  a statement within a couple of days so  at least they're keeping us informed  royal commentator richard fitzwilliams  thinks the queen will be eager to get  back to work obviously her medical team  led by sir thomas are keeping a very  close eye on the on matters the palace  has not said when she will resume online  public duties from thursday people in  england with covid no longer need to  isolate but are advised to do so if they  can redmond shannon global news windsor  england  ahead a landmark win for the u.s women's  soccer team  in the u.s three men convicted of  murdering ahmed arbury who was unarmed  have been found guilty on all charges  the jury took less than four hours to 